llvm-3.7.1 local rule: an ordered atomic read-modify-write does not modify
a frame object that nothing before it captured or was handed to write
(no upstream state)

This patch CHANGES MEMORY DEPENDENCE ONLY (AliasAnalysis::
callCapturesBefore, which MemoryDependenceAnalysis asks as its fallback for
an instruction that getModRefInfo calls ModRef, MemoryDependenceAnalysis.cpp
:619-621). One change, nothing else:
  AliasAnalysis.cpp, callCapturesBefore: for an atomicrmw or a cmpxchg (ModRef
    for any ordering above monotonic, AliasAnalysis.cpp:335-346 and the
    cmpxchg form above it) the answer is NoModRef when the queried location's
    underlying object is an identified local object, it is not captured
    before the atomic (PointerMayBeCapturedBefore, the call's own test), no
    call that may reach the atomic is given a pointer based on it for an
    argument it may write through (a call other than an intrinsic whose
    parameter is neither readonly nor readnone and that is not
    onlyReadsMemory), and the atomic's own pointer is NoAlias with the
    object; ModRef otherwise.
Unchanged: every answer for a call (the existing path); getModRefInfo of an
atomic itself (a client that asks it directly, such as LICM's alias sets,
sees the ordered atomic as before; memory dependence's users, GVN and DSE,
take the rule); a monotonic or relaxed atomic (already answered by alias
alone); fences. The library line (3.3) is another
compiler. src/sce/ and src/game/sndx/ are built by this compiler and take the
rule.

Question (rounds 549E, 551E, 553E, 554E, 557E): the base keeps a frame
Name's index in a register across the Name's own seq_cst `lock xadd` where
3.7.1 reloads it for the free (FUN_00489c30's one divergence: `mov edi,
r14d` in the base, `mov edi, [rbp-0xb8]` in the build), and still reloads at
other sites. Base census (scratch e553/relscan4.txt): 2,878 sites in 314
functions keep the index across a call taking the slot's address and then
across the xadd; 1,675 sites in 158 functions reload after both; no site
keeps across one and reloads across the other. The opt of every release
from 3.7.1 to 9.0.0 keeps the reload (round 553E).

Evidence (scratch e554/, e557/, e561/). The module built in both stages with
the line's patches and this one, against a control built by the same script
with the installed compiler (equal to the tree's module in every symbol):
  14 symbols change, 0 matched rows change (0 rows lost); 4 drafts equal
    (FUN_00489c30, FUN_005fb120, FUN_008af940, Object016abc00's C2), 1
    closer (FUN_008acb00 0.07 to 0.69); the five setText lambdas of
    FUN_0088b4e0 lose their reload after the xadd as in the base and score
    lower on register names and the decrement's place.
  Reload sites: all 103 direct-call and memory-indirect sites read (e557
    s1/step1_table.txt): 103 of 103 predicted. In each the slot is written
    by a call taking its address that the base reloads after, or the
    address is stored.
  Keep sites: a sample of 60, one per function, evenly over the 314 (e557
    s1/K60b.txt, K60c.txt): 59 of 59 predicted (one is a Name held in a
    register, not a slot). In each the value got into the slot by the
    caller's own store and every later call taking the address is one the
    base keeps across.
  Keep sites with an earlier capturing use of the same frame slot: 406
    (174 in a loop with it). Read (e561/ka.txt; by hand a sample of
    thirty over the five large functions and ten others, and the nine
    takers of the 83): every one is a different object, 323 an earlier
    Name temporary passed to a virtual call and released, its slot zeroed,
    right after it, before the kept Name is built; 83 of another type (a
    std::function's buffer, a bool captured by a lambda, 16-byte vectors
    and a record); 0 against.
  The rule without its second clause (round 554E's atomic-01): FUN_00ed7980
    (sndx, a spill reused across a cmpxchg) moves away, and 0x5f2490 and
    0x1348360 (FUN_00c91140 writes the index through a nocapture
    out-parameter) and 0x614fb0 are against it. 0x885840 and 0x886300,
    counted against it in round 557E, are for both forms: the frame element
    pushed there has its counted reference exchanged in place (`lock
    cmpxchg qword [r14]`, r14 = rbp-0x58, at 0x885aa7 and 0x886567), and
    3.7.1's CaptureTracking takes a cmpxchg's pointer as a capture (its
    default case), so the element is captured before the Name's xadd in
    every iteration (e561/probe: the reload kept under this rule). The push
    itself, FUN_008a9550 (a matched row), only loads through its argument.

Source forms the bytes exclude (rounds 551E, 553E): the drop relaxed (110
to 1,253 rows lost); release() reading the index once (the rowed
Name::~Name at 0x1331800 reloads `this->index`); the Name passed by value
(the caller's IR is the same under the Itanium ABI: no change); the index
copied to a second slot (the base has one slot, its address passed and
zeroed after the release).

NO upstream state. Every release from 3.7.1 to 9.0.0 answers ModRef for an
ordered atomic here. Sony authorship of this is not shown.

Refuted by: a matched row, or a base site read in full, where a frame object
reaches an ordered atomic on another address having been passed only to
calls the base keeps it across, and is reloaded after the atomic; or one
kept across the atomic after a call the base reloads it after.

